API-13: take a wet runoff step while API rainfall is set on a subcatchment

runoff_getTimeStep() uses WET_STEP only when IsRaining (a gage reports
rain), HasSnow, HasRunoff or HasWetLids is set. Rainfall or snowfall set on
a subcatchment with swmm_SUBCATCH_API_RAINFALL / _API_SNOWFALL is added to
the subcatchment in getNetPrecip() but did not set IsRaining, so with a dry
gage the runoff step was DRY_STEP (limited only by the gage's next value):
one long step computed with the rate in force at its start. Set IsRaining
when any subcatchment has a positive API rainfall or snowfall.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-13_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
index bf00bad..3c43116 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
@@ -201,6 +201,14 @@ void runoff_execute()
         if ( Gage[j].rainfall > 0.0 ) IsRaining = TRUE;
     }
 
+    // --- precipitation set on a subcatchment through the API also
+    //     requires a wet time step
+    for (j = 0; j < Nobjects[SUBCATCH]; j++)
+    {
+        if ( Subcatch[j].apiRainfall > 0.0 || Subcatch[j].apiSnowfall > 0.0 )
+            IsRaining = TRUE;
+    }
+
     // --- read runoff results from interface file if applicable
     if ( Frunoff.mode == USE_FILE )
     {
